#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:16
msgid "How to upload Sketch to the Board?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:18
msgid "In this section, you will learn how to upload the sketch created previously to the Arduino board, as well as learn about some considerations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:20
msgid "**1. Choose Board and port**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:22
msgid "Arduino development boards usually come with a USB cable. You can use it to connect the board to your computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:24
msgid "Select the correct **Board** and **Port** in the Arduino IDE. Normally, Arduino boards are recognized automatically by the computer and assigned a port, so you can select it here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:30
msgid "If your board is already plugged in, but not recognized, check if the **INSTALLED** logo appears in the **Arduino AVR Boards** section of the **Boards Manager**, if not, please scroll down a bit and click on **INSTALL**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:35
msgid "Specifically, for UNO R4, search **\"UNO R4\"** in **Boards Manager** and check if the corresponding library is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:40
msgid "Reopening the Arduino IDE and re-plugging the Arduino board will fix most of the problems. You can also click **Tools** -> **Board** or **Port** to select them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:43
msgid "**2. Verify the Sketch**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:45
msgid "After clicking the Verify button, the sketch will be compiled to see if there are any errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:50
msgid "You can use it to find mistakes if you delete some characters or type a few letters by mistake. From the message bar, you can see where and what type of errors occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:55
msgid "If there are no errors, you will see a message like the one below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:61
msgid "**3. Upload sketch**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:63
msgid "After completing the above steps, click the **Upload** button to upload this sketch to the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:68
msgid "If successful, you will be able to see the following prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:73
msgid "At the same time, the on-board LED blink."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/04_basic_upload.rst:83
msgid "The Arduino board will automatically run the sketch after power is applied after the sketch is uploaded. The running program can be overwritten by uploading a new sketch."
msgstr ""
